 time admitting i didn't  know anything about nutrition i taxed my  body and my brain bore the brunt of it  for a while i just felt very anxious and  very lost at that time this wasn't the  first time hathaway suffered for the  sake of her art for her role as catwoman  in the dark knight rises she dieted and  worked out extensively she admitted to  elora that her efforts to fit into the  cat suit dominated her life for a year  explaining i didn't understand how you  could be thin and strong i went into the  gym for 10 months and i didn't come out  as a despairing cocaine addict and the  partner of an unpredictable and  hot-headed gangster elvira hancock from  brian depalma's scarface has the sort of  energy that's eating her alive from the  inside out naturally actress michelle  pfeiffer wanted to embody the tragic  heroine in all her raging authenticity  and that involved shedding some pounds  people reports that pfeiffer lived on a  diet of marlboros and tomato soup to  play the love interest of the  larger-than-life tony montana pfeiffer  said i was playing a cocaine addict so  that was part of the physicality of the  park as production continued pfeiffer  became thinner and more emaciated the  actress recalled that what was  originally planned as a three-month  movie shoot ended up dragging along for  twice that time elaborating i was  starving by the end of it because the  one scene that was the end of the film  where i needed to be my thinnest it was  pushed to the next week and then it was  the next week and then it was the next  week i literally had members of the crew  bringing me bagels because they were all  worried about me and how thin i was  getting  when lily collins lost weight to play a  young woman with anorexia in the netflix  movie to the bone it was a harrowing  experience the actress had suffered from  eating disorders in the past and  although she had a doctor on board to  ensure she lost weight safely it was  still a difficult process fought with  anxiety the actress explained to al how  apprehensive she was about stepping back  into shoes that contained nothing but  negative experiences for her colin said  you're doing it for a part but it's  something so close to you there's a fine  line between are you going to fall back  into it are you not  collins insisted that playing the role  for the greater purpose of highlighting  the condition gave her strength and  inner resolve she explained to glamour  that she lost 20 pounds under the  watchful eye of a nutritionist who gave  her lots of supplements she elaborated  we really made sure to maintain a  semblance of control over the situation  and also just to make sure my body was  functioning the way that it should i was  reminding myself daily that i was hired  as an actor not because of the body i  would have attained by suffering  playing an emaciated aids patient isn't  really possible unless you look the part  and matthew mcconaughey certainly put in  a strong effort when it came to losing  weight for the role of ron woodruff in  dallas buyer's club the actor followed a  very unique diet during his preparation  for the project  what were you eating honestly five  ounces of fish cup of vegetables twice a  day  some pudding in the morning and as much  red wine as i liked at night  the actor told the independent about the  effects of his weight loss saying i got  down to 143 pounds and i was always  hungry and irritable my body resembled a  baby bird with its mouth open crying  feed me feed me and you realize mama  bird ain't going to feed you it's hard  mcconaughey wasn't alone in his dieting  health for dallas buyers club to play  the role of a transgender aids patient  named rayon his co-star jared leto lost  40 pounds when asked by the rap how he  did it leto simply replied i stopped  eating it wasn't an easy thing to do  losing that much weight changes the way  you walk the way you sit the way you  think  traditionally the joker has never been a  partly villain his trusted mind and  psychotic personality move fast and  without any excess baggage the caped  crusaders nemesis has never been meaner  or leaner than in 2019's joker and it's  all thanks to joaquin phoenix's mental  and physical transformation into one of  dc comics greatest characters phoenix's  unique take on the tragic clown is more  nihilistic more insane more sinister and  more human than any other version the  joker's wired and angular personality  his uncontrollable tics and his nervous  energy are all captured in phoenix's  oscar-winning performance before he  could film it though he had to shed 52  pounds for the role phoenix believes the  weight loss enhanced his performance but  admitted to the new york times it's a  horrible way to live warner brothers  production notes state that phoenix  achieved that starved and unhealthy look  by eating little more than an apple a  day which didn't make him feel great at  first in the beginning  you're exhausted  i mean sometimes you look at a flight of  stairs and it takes like 30 seconds you  have to talk yourself into it  by the end of the extreme diet however  he was feeling quote energized and  excited still the process took a toll on  his mind he explained at the venice film  festival it turns out that affects your  psychology you start to go mad how  fitting for the clown prince of crime  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stars are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

